 would speak over this loud  god Mike and all the nursing staff would  freeze his third day in the hospital  Burstein says was his worst on a trip to  the bathroom he found himself gasping  for breath again and I you know and I'd  had that scary moment in this tiny  little bathroom thinking oh god this is  not the way it's can't end this way  in this stupid bathroom when no one's  gonna know I'm in here he staggered back  to his room and told a nurse and I was  sputtering I couldn't breathe  besides not being able to breathe are  you okay tell you not to panic everybody  was in the same boat exactly and she I'm  sure and I'm sure she'd seen much worse  so her nonchalant attitude made me relax  actually you had a pair of doctors who  had names that you said were very  comforting to you yes one was named dr.  Gandhi and the other ones named dr.  Krishna and they were both kind and  smart and comforting and I greatly  appreciate their expertise after five  days in the hospital Burstein finally  was discharged how did it feel to walk  out the door it felt surreal  like I wasn't sure that it would happen  when I left my apartment building when I  left the lobby I prayed that it wouldn't  be the last time that I was seeing my  lobby do you feel mentally now that  you've been through all this I feel a  little fragile but incredibly grateful  at the same time grateful for my breath  it told me that I'm now immune so  tribulations yeah so I'm like a freakin  superhero you think you'll be back on  Broadway someday hell yes absolutely we  will how we will is yet to be discovered  when I tell you the first the first  night you're back on the stage that's  gonna be a heck of a night it is  is I can't wait and I feel sorry for the  first guy who costs in the audience when  Danny Burstein is back on back on  Broadway rushed to see Danny Burstein  when he's back on Broadway because he's  terrific so is his wife Rebecca lucre  they're both amazing performers and  singers she by the way had the  coronavirus as well not as severely and  she's doing fine now so that's a that's  a recovery story that that is really  nice to hear yes oh Anthony I can't say  enough about Danny Burstein  I can't wait to see him on Broadway on  stage again number one his story was so  descriptive which I liked because we so  take breathing for granted and for him  to spell it out the way he did I felt  like we were all there with him I also  loved how he gave a shout-out to his  doctors kind and gentle and smart just  another reminder about the work that the  people are doing and people like Danny  are surviving because of it oh what a  great great interview
 

